---
import GuideLayout from '../../../layouts/GuideLayout.astro';
const toc=[
  {href:'#overview',label:'Overview'},
  {href:'#skills',label:'Skills'},
  {href:'#enchant',label:'Skill Enchantment'},
  {href:'#buffs',label:'Buffs'},
  {href:'#status',label:'Character Status'},
  {href:'#details',label:'Combat Stats Info'},
  {href:'#stats',label:'Base Stats'},
  {href:'#elixirs',label:'Elixirs'},
  {href:'#builds',label:'Stat Recommendations'},
  {href:'#mistakes',label:'Common Mistakes'}
];
---
<GuideLayout title="Character | L2 Guardian Guides" lang="en" active="character" toc={toc}>
<div class="content">
  <a class="back" href="/en/">← Back to home</a>
  <section class="hero"><img src="/images/character-stat-breakpoints.png" alt="Character Status and Stat Bonus windows in L2 Reborn Guardian"/><div class="hero-body"><div class="badge">CHARACTER SYSTEM</div><h1>Character</h1><p class="subtitle">Learn skills, automate buffs, enchant abilities and distribute stats around the breakpoints that provide the greatest benefit to your build.</p><div class="info-grid"><div class="info-card"><div class="label">Skill Window</div><div class="value">K</div></div><div class="info-card"><div class="label">Character Window</div><div class="value">T</div></div><div class="info-card"><div class="label">Base Buff Slots</div><div class="value">24</div></div><div class="info-card"><div class="label">Maximum Elixirs</div><div class="value">29</div></div></div></div></section>

  <section class="section quick-start"><div class="quick-head"><div class="quick-icon">✦</div><div><h2>Quick Start</h2><p>The most important character management rules.</p></div></div><div class="quick-grid"><div class="quick-card"><div class="quick-title">Magical Goal</div><div class="quick-value">90 INT + 50 WIT</div><span class="quick-tag high">Check Breakpoints</span></div><div class="quick-card"><div class="quick-title">Physical Goal</div><div class="quick-value">90 STR + 60 DEX</div><span class="quick-tag high">Check Breakpoints</span></div><div class="quick-card"><div class="quick-title">Buff Capacity</div><div class="quick-value">24 to 28</div><span class="quick-tag medium">Divine Inspiration</span></div><div class="quick-card"><div class="quick-title">Stat Reset</div><div class="quick-value">500k Adena</div><span class="quick-tag medium">All Extra Points</span></div></div><div class="quick-footer"><div class="quick-tip"><strong>Inspect before investing</strong>Open Stat Bonus and Combat Stats Info before distributing points.</div><div class="quick-tip"><strong>Automate long buffs</strong>Place them on the shortcut bar and use the right mouse button.</div><div class="quick-tip"><strong>Plan for chapters</strong>Some Spellbook rarities remain unavailable until later content.</div></div></section>

  <section class="section" id="overview"><h2>Overview</h2><p>The Character systems connect skills, buffs, Skill Enchantment, basic attributes, Elixirs and the detailed combat stat panel. Improving only the visible P. Atk. or M. Atk. value is not enough. Attribute breakpoints and hidden combat modifiers can change the most efficient upgrade for a build.</p><p>This guide is not limited to Chapter 1. Availability notes explain which Spellbooks and features unlock as Guardian progresses through later chapters.</p></section>

  <section class="section" id="skills"><h2>Skills</h2><p>Press <strong>K</strong>, or open Menu and select Skills. The Character tab separates Active, Passive and Available skills. The Item tab contains abilities learned through objects, while Enchant lists skills that can be improved.</p><p>Learn a new skill from Character > Available when its level and item requirements are satisfied. Depending on the ability, the fee can require Magic Tablets or a Spellbook of a specific rarity.</p><div class="guide-gallery"><figure><img src="/images/character-skills-overview.png" alt="Active skills and buffs in the Skills window"/><figcaption>Skills include active abilities, passives, toggles, buffs, debuffs and transformations.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="/images/character-skills-available.png" alt="Available skill with its Spellbook requirement"/><figcaption>Available shows the requirements and the Learn Skills button.</figcaption></figure></div><h3>Spellbooks and Ancient Adena</h3><p>Magic Tablets and Spellbooks are sold in the <strong>Merchant of Mammon</strong> section of the L Coin Store. Purchases use Ancient Adena, obtained by farming in Catacombs and completing these missions:</p><table><thead><tr><th>Source</th><th>Frequency</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Catacomb farming</td><td>While farming</td></tr><tr><td>Catacomb Raider</td><td>Daily mission</td></tr><tr><td>Seven Signs Inquisitor</td><td>Weekly mission</td></tr></tbody></table><figure class="guide-figure wide"><img src="/images/character-mammon-spellbooks.png" alt="Spellbooks sold by Merchant of Mammon"/><figcaption>Book rarity, price and purchase limits are displayed directly in the store.</figcaption></figure><div class="note"><strong>Chapter progression:</strong> Chapter 1 allowed the purchase of only one Rare Spellbook. This limit is removed in Chapter 2, but Heroic Spellbooks are still unavailable.</div></section>

  <section class="section" id="enchant"><h2>Skill Enchantment</h2><div class="steps"><div class="step"><div class="num">1</div><div><strong>Open Skills > Enchant</strong><p>Select a compatible skill with the right mouse button and click Skill Enchantment.</p></div></div><div class="step"><div class="num">2</div><div><strong>Fill the progress bar</strong><p>Add Magic Tablets, Spellbooks or SP Pouches, then press Drain. Drained materials are consumed immediately and contribute points until the bar reaches 100%.</p></div></div><div class="step"><div class="num">3</div><div><strong>Attempt the enchant</strong><p>Review the current effect, next level result, Adena fee and success rate before confirming.</p></div></div></div><div class="guide-gallery"><figure><img src="/images/character-skill-enchant-entry.png" alt="Opening Skill Enchantment from the Enchant tab"/><figcaption>Only compatible learned skills appear in this section.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="/images/character-skill-enchant.png" alt="Skill Enchantment progress and success rate"/><figcaption>The point requirement and success chance vary by enchant level.</figcaption></figure></div><h3>SP Pouch Craft</h3><p>Click the pouch icon with a plus sign inside Skill Enchantment to craft SP Pouches. The shown recipe costs 50,000,000 SP and 10,000,000 Adena, with a limit of ten craft attempts per day.</p><figure class="guide-figure compact"><img src="/images/character-sp-pouch.png" alt="SP Pouch craft cost and daily limit"/><figcaption>SP Pouches provide another material source for filling enchant progress.</figcaption></figure><h3>Failure Protection</h3><p>A failed enchant keeps the current skill level and grants Skill Enchant XP toward the next attempt. The reward increases by 90,000 points for every consecutive failure:</p><table><thead><tr><th>Failures in a Row</th><th>Skill Enchant XP</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>90,000</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>180,000</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>270,000</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>360,000</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>450,000</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>540,000</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>630,000</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td>720,000</td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td>810,000</td></tr><tr><td>10</td><td>900,000</td></tr></tbody></table><p>The failure count can reach ten. If the skill fails more than ten consecutive times, the counter returns to one.</p></section>

  <section class="section" id="buffs"><h2>Buffs</h2><p>Buffs are learned in the Buffs section of the Skills window. Most last 20 minutes. Some class specific buffs have a shorter duration but provide stronger effects. Casting consumes Spirit Ores, and the required amount depends on the buff.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Capacity</th><th>Maximum Buffs</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Base character</td><td>24</td></tr><tr><td>Divine Inspiration Lv. 4</td><td>28</td></tr></tbody></table><p>To automate a buff, place it on the shortcut bar and use the right mouse button. A bright border appears around the icon when automatic use is active. Applied buffs are displayed in the normal buff bar.</p><div class="guide-gallery effects"><figure><img src="/images/character-buffs.png" alt="Buff section in the Skills window"/><figcaption>Learned character buffs appear with the other active skills.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="/images/character-auto-buffs.png" alt="Buff shortcuts enabled for automatic use"/><figcaption>The bright border marks buffs configured for automatic use.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="/images/character-active-buffs.png" alt="Active character buff bar"/><figcaption>Active effects remain visible in the buff bar.</figcaption></figure></div></section>

  <section class="section" id="status"><h2>Character Status and Combat Power</h2><p>Press <strong>T</strong>, or click the Character icon near the lower right interface, to open Character Status. The main panel displays HP, MP, CP, SP, P. Atk., M. Atk., P. Def., M. Def., Atk. Spd., Casting Spd. and Speed.</p><p>Combat Power appears in the upper right. Hover over it to see how much comes from Equipment, Doll effects, Doll Collections, Aden Laboratory and other contributing systems.</p><div class="guide-gallery"><figure><img src="/images/character-button.png" alt="Character button in the lower interface"/><figcaption>The Character icon provides an alternative to the T shortcut.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="/images/character-combat-power.png" alt="Character Status and Combat Power breakdown"/><figcaption>Hover over Combat Power to identify where every point originates.</figcaption></figure></div></section>

  <section class="section" id="details"><h2>Combat Stats Info</h2><p>Click <strong>Details</strong> beside Combat Stats to open the complete stat breakdown. Categories include Attack, Defense, Accuracy, Evasion, Speed, Critical Rate, Critical Damage, Recovery, Skill Cooldown, MP Consumption and Anomalies.</p><p>The panel separates percentage modifiers from numerical values and includes PvE, PvP, Soulshot, Spiritshot, Skill Power, weapon bonuses and many other modifiers. Hover over a row to read what the stat affects and how its value is calculated.</p><div class="guide-gallery"><figure><img src="/images/character-combat-details.png" alt="Combat Stats Info categories and attack values"/><figcaption>Details exposes modifiers that are not visible in the basic Character Status list.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="/images/character-combat-tooltip.png" alt="Combat stat explanatory tooltip"/><figcaption>Use the tooltips when comparing similarly named percentages and numerical stats.</figcaption></figure></div></section>

  <section class="section" id="stats"><h2>Base Stats and Breakpoints</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Stat</th><th>Main Effects</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>STR</strong></td><td>P. Atk.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>INT</strong></td><td>M. Atk.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>DEX</strong></td><td>Attack Speed and Basic Critical Rate</td></tr><tr><td><strong>WIT</strong></td><td>Casting Speed, Magic Skill Critical Rate and Magic Damage Resistance</td></tr><tr><td><strong>CON</strong></td><td>HP and CP, recovery, weight limit, breath gauge and Shield Defense Rate</td></tr><tr><td><strong>MEN</strong></td><td>Magic Defense, Max MP, MP Recovery Rate and Casting Interruption Rate</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Hover over a base stat to review its effects. Click <strong>Stat Bonus</strong> to see the bonuses unlocked at specific thresholds. These breakpoints can be more valuable than adding points to the primary stat without reaching its next reward.</p><div class="example"><strong>Breakpoint example</strong><p>WIT 40 grants M. Critical Rate +50, WIT 50 grants Magic Skill Cooldown +10%, and MEN 45 grants M. Def. +200. If 90 INT is currently unreachable, reaching 50 WIT can provide a stronger immediate result.</p></div><div class="guide-gallery wide"><figure><img src="/images/character-stat-breakpoints.png" alt="Character base stat breakpoints"/><figcaption>Stat Bonus shows every available threshold and highlights those already active.</figcaption></figure></div><h3>Verify the Real Result</h3><p>After reaching a breakpoint, open Combat Stats Info and compare the affected value. In the provided example, reaching 50 WIT increases the numerical M. Skill Critical Rate from 4 to 9.</p><div class="guide-gallery"><figure><img src="/images/character-wit-before.png" alt="Magic Skill Critical Rate before 50 WIT"/><figcaption>Before 50 WIT: M. Skill Critical Rate 4.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="/images/character-wit-after.png" alt="Magic Skill Critical Rate after 50 WIT"/><figcaption>After 50 WIT: M. Skill Critical Rate 9.</figcaption></figure></div></section>

  <section class="section" id="elixirs"><h2>Elixirs</h2><p>Craft Elixirs through Special Craft > Upgrade / Growth > Upgrade. One attempt consumes ten Elixir Powders and has a 50% chance to produce one Elixir. A failed craft returns three Elixir Powders.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Elixir Powder Source</th><th>Daily Amount</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Assault on Elmoreden Tower</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>Elmoreden Lady</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Each consumed Elixir grants one additional base stat point. The usage limit begins at five Elixirs from levels 76 to 85 and rises with character level until reaching 29 at level 97 or higher.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Level</th><th>Maximum Elixirs</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>76 to 85</td><td>5</td></tr><tr><td>86</td><td>7</td></tr><tr><td>87</td><td>9</td></tr><tr><td>88</td><td>11</td></tr><tr><td>89</td><td>13</td></tr><tr><td>90</td><td>15</td></tr><tr><td>91</td><td>17</td></tr><tr><td>92</td><td>19</td></tr><tr><td>93</td><td>21</td></tr><tr><td>94</td><td>23</td></tr><tr><td>95</td><td>25</td></tr><tr><td>96</td><td>27</td></tr><tr><td>97 or higher</td><td>29</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="guide-gallery"><figure><img src="/images/character-elixir-craft.png" alt="Elixir recipe in Special Craft"/><figcaption>The recipe shows both the Elixir success and Powder return outcomes.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="/images/character-elixir-limits.png" alt="Elixir level based usage limits"/><figcaption>The tooltip lists the maximum Elixirs allowed at every level.</figcaption></figure></div><h3>Resetting Stat Points</h3><p>Reset costs 500,000 Adena and returns every additional stat point at the current level. This includes points earned through leveling and points supplied by Elixirs. The points are not lost and can be distributed again.</p><figure class="guide-figure compact"><img src="/images/character-stat-reset.png" alt="Stat point reset confirmation and Adena cost"/><figcaption>The confirmation window states that level and Elixir points are reset together.</figcaption></figure></section>

  <section class="section" id="builds"><h2>Recommended Stat Goals</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Character Type</th><th>Primary Goal</th><th>Secondary Goal</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Magical</strong></td><td>90 INT</td><td>50 WIT</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Physical</strong></td><td>90 STR</td><td>60 DEX</td></tr></tbody></table><p>These are progression goals, not a reason to ignore reachable breakpoints. If the primary target is not currently possible, invest in a secondary threshold that activates a useful bonus, then redistribute later for 500,000 Adena when additional points become available.</p></section>

  <section class="section" id="mistakes"><h2>Common Mistakes</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Mistake</th><th>Why It Hurts</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Distributing points without opening Stat Bonus</td><td class="bad">You may stop just below a powerful breakpoint or invest toward an unreachable one.</td></tr><tr><td>Checking only the basic Character Status values</td><td>Important PvE, PvP, Skill Power and critical modifiers remain hidden in Combat Stats Info.</td></tr><tr><td>Draining enchant materials before reviewing the requirement</td><td>Materials are consumed as soon as Drain is pressed.</td></tr><tr><td>Ignoring Spirit Ore consumption</td><td>Automated buffs can stop when the required consumables run out.</td></tr><tr><td>Assuming a failed Elixir craft loses all ten Powders</td><td>The failure result returns three Powders.</td></tr></tbody></table></section>
</div>
</GuideLayout>
